Deferral does not convert missing public evidence into an accepted proof. Until the release is actually published and independently verified, all of the following remain pending:

- successful Trusted Publisher execution for the intended release;
- exact public wheel/sdist identity;
- no-cache installation of the exact public package;
- public Linux/macOS/Windows MCP verification;
- P0.6 closure.

- discovers current reviewable project-doc candidates;
- removes orphaned indexed docs whose files were deleted or are no longer discovered;
- removes stale indexed sections for changed files;
- indexes new and changed reviewable docs;
- verifies the final indexed state before reporting results.

## Docs MCP server

`doc-atlas mcp docs-serve` runs the local Docs MCP server. Find the command with `doc-atlas --help` followed by `doc-atlas mcp --help`.

Its public workflow has exactly three tools:

- `get_docs_context` — first documentation question;
- `prepare_docs` — a returned or explicitly approved sync/prefetch action;
- `docs_status` — a returned job, health, or freshness request.
